Unit tests are great, favor them if they don't require mocks or stubs.
From there, use integration tests for testing interactions between components.
End-to-end (E2E) tests should focus exclusively on real user journeys and visible outcomes. Only assert on navigation, visible UI elements, and user-facing messages. Do not assert on implementation details, internal state, localStorage, or console output. Do not attempt to test third-party flows (e.g., Google OAuth); instead, use helpers to simulate logged-in or logged-out states.

State setup: Use Cypress helpers (e.g., `cy.loginAsTestUser()`, `cy.logout()`, `cy.stubGoogleLogin()`) to simulate authentication states for E2E tests.

Cover both happy and unhappy paths.

Do not assert against specific CSS values or HTML elements. Focus on functionality and content.

Let's try to honor the traditional test pyramid.
We strongly discourage mocks and stubs. Avoid if at all possible.
